WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.773
The temple was high on a hill, and it was a clear day, so Brody could see far into the distance.

2
00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:15.606
And yet nothing he saw looked familiar. What had happened to the school and playing fields?

3
00:00:15.607 --> 00:00:19.299
Where were the houses and his favorite fast-food place?

4
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:25.156
"What's going on?" he blurted out. "Where are we? Where's the gym?"

5
00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:30.275
"The gymnasium? It's right over there, of course." Hermes pointed to the left.

6
00:00:30.276 --> 00:00:34.600
But Brody still didn't see anything that looked like the school gym.

7
00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:42.602
"It can't be," Julia murmured. "Are we really in ancient Olympia?"

8
00:00:42.603 --> 00:00:47.640
"What?" Brody said. "There's no way we traveled through time."

9
00:00:47.641 --> 00:00:53.905
Julia was staring at the city below. "What other explanation is there?"

10
00:00:53.906 --> 00:01:02.276
Brody rolled his eyes. People thought he was dumb, but he wasn't dumb enough to believe what Hermes and Caerus were saying.

11
00:01:02.277 --> 00:01:08.771
Only a freak like Julia would believe such a ridiculous story. Ancient Greece? Yeah, right!

12
00:01:08.772 --> 00:01:12.624
Still, there was definitely something weird going on.

13
00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:16.395
How could Brody make Hermes and Caerus admit it?

14
00:01:16.396 --> 00:01:21.794
"I've got it!" He pointed at Hermes. "You're lying, and I can prove it."

15
00:01:21.795 --> 00:01:26.087
Hermes raised one eyebrow. "Is that so?"

16
00:01:26.088 --> 00:01:34.044
"Yes. If we're in Greece, how come you guys are speaking English?" Brody was proud of himself.

17
00:01:34.045 --> 00:01:38.791
He might not be a genius, but he could figure things out when he needed to.

18
00:01:38.792 --> 00:01:44.097
"On the contrary, we're speaking proper Greek," Caerus said.

19
00:01:44.098 --> 00:01:47.215
"Hermes has powers over language and communication.

20
00:01:47.216 --> 00:01:52.172
He has enabled you two to speak and understand Greek as if you were natives." Hermes

21
00:01:52.173 --> 00:02:00.446
smirked. "That's very important. After all, speaking Greek is a prerequisite for entering the Games." "Huh?"

22
00:02:00.447 --> 00:02:04.619
Brody didn't know what "prerequisite" meant. Before

23
00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:09.940
he could ask, Caerus glanced at Hermes and pantomimed eating. "Yes,

24
00:02:09.941 --> 00:02:14.691
this conversation is becoming dull," Hermes said to his friend. He

25
00:02:14.692 --> 00:02:21.975
turned to Brody and Julia. "If you're still confused, your mortal hosts can explain everything." "You'll

26
00:02:21.976 --> 00:02:25.403
be staying with the family that tends my temple." Caerus

27
00:02:25.404 --> 00:02:29.884
waved a hand to indicate the temple they had just exited. "Let's

28
00:02:29.885 --> 00:02:32.472
go," Hermes ordered. Brody

29
00:02:32.473 --> 00:02:40.404
was more confused than ever. And being confused made him mad. "I'm

30
00:02:40.405 --> 00:02:45.029
not going anywhere with you!" He gave Hermes a shove. "You're

31
00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:49.235
not gods. You're just jerks and fakers!" Suddenly

32
00:02:49.236 --> 00:02:57.424
a loud, chilling cry seemed to rip the air in two. At

33
00:02:57.425 --> 00:03:09.083
the same moment, Hermes transformed into an enormous hawk and dived at Brody. The

34
00:03:09.084 --> 00:03:13.751
hawk's giant talons stopped a hair's breadth from Brody's face. Brody

35
00:03:13.752 --> 00:03:21.002
fell back, gasping with fear. A second later Hermes looked normal again. "Learn

36
00:03:21.003 --> 00:03:25.774
this lesson well, mortal!" Hermes said sternly. "Do

37
00:03:25.775 --> 00:03:30.274
not defy me! I can be either your friend or your enemy. Trust

38
00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:33.921
me, you'd rather have me as a friend." "Come."

39
00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:39.956
Caerus headed down the steps of his temple. "Your hosts are waiting." Brody

40
00:03:39.957 --> 00:03:48.483
opened his mouth to argue again, but Hermes was still glaring at him. "Fine," Brody muttered. Caerus

41
00:03:48.484 --> 00:03:52.510
led the way to a modest home halfway down the hill. A

42
00:03:52.511 --> 00:03:56.615
bearded man wearing a purple robe stood in front. "Welcome,

43
00:03:56.616 --> 00:04:05.071
Caerus," the man said, bowing. "We are honored by your presence. Yours as well, Hermes." "Thank

44
00:04:05.072 --> 00:04:12.234
you," Hermes said. "Caerus tells me you've agreed to look after my champion until the Games." "Of

45
00:04:12.235 --> 00:04:20.638
course." The man bowed to Brody. "My name is Nikolaos. My eldest son will take care of your needs." A

46
00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:24.019
boy around Brody's age stepped outside. Like

47
00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:32.500
the men he wore one of those strange-looking chitons. "Hi," he said shyly. "I'm Markos." "Hey."

48
00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:39.468
Brody nodded. "I'm Brody." Julia stepped forward. "I'm Julia." "Oh,

49
00:04:39.469 --> 00:04:47.554
right," Caerus said. "We'll also need you to look after the champion's . . . companion ."

50
00:04:47.555 --> 00:04:52.405
"A girl ?" Nikolaos stared at Julia, and then

51
00:04:52.406 --> 00:04:56.724
shrugged. "As you wish, Caerus. We can always use help in the

52
00:04:56.725 --> 00:05:04.665
kitchen." Julia frowned, but she didn't say anything. Soon the two gods

53
00:05:04.666 --> 00:05:08.443
left. "Take care of our guests, Markos," Nikolaos

54
00:05:08.444 --> 00:05:11.430
said. "I have important work to do at the

55
00:05:11.431 --> 00:05:15.444
temple." "Yes, Father," Markos said as Nikolaos

56
00:05:15.445 --> 00:05:19.665
left. Brody quickly glanced at Julia. "I'm going back to the

57
00:05:19.666 --> 00:05:24.869
temple. Caerus and Hermes said we could get home through that crack in the wall, so that's what I'm

58
00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:32.110
doing." "What?" Markos looked alarmed. "You can't leave! Hermes will be

59
00:05:32.111 --> 00:05:35.256
angry." Brody shrugged. "So

60
00:05:35.257 --> 00:05:40.676
what?" Markos shook his head. "Hermes may seem good-natured, but he is still a god.

61
00:05:40.677 --> 00:05:47.326
As you know, gods aren't like mortals, and they think nothing of punishing us at their whim."

62
00:05:47.327 --> 00:05:55.081
"How would I know that?" Brody said. "Up until a few minutes ago, I didn't know gods really existed."

63
00:05:55.082 --> 00:05:59.270
Markos looked confused. "What do you mean?"

64
00:05:59.271 --> 00:06:06.560
"Listen, Markos." Julia jumped in. "What's all this talk about Brody being Hermes' champion?

65
00:06:06.561 --> 00:06:09.766
And are the Olympic Games really starting soon?"

66
00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:15.892
Her questions tumbled out. "Is Hermes really a god? I mean, for real?"

67
00:06:15.893 --> 00:06:21.596
Markos stared at her. "You ask many questions for a girl."

68
00:06:21.597 --> 00:06:32.810
Julia looked annoyed. Brody almost laughed, but he wanted to know the answer to her questions too. "Just answer her," he told Markos.

69
00:06:32.811 --> 00:06:37.493
"Yes, the Olympic Games begin soon," Markos said.

70
00:06:37.494 --> 00:06:44.152
"Every four years all the gods compete to see who can find the best mortal athlete."

71
00:06:44.153 --> 00:06:48.736
He shook his head. "But you must already know that."

72
00:06:48.737 --> 00:06:54.327
"No, we don't," Julia said. "We came from the future."

73
00:06:54.328 --> 00:06:57.829
"The future? I don't understand."

74
00:06:57.830 --> 00:07:02.547
"Wait . . ." Brody had just realized what Markos meant.

75
00:07:02.548 --> 00:07:07.153
"So Hermes thinks I'm the best athlete around?"

76
00:07:07.154 --> 00:07:11.282
Markos shrugged. "I suppose so."

77
00:07:11.283 --> 00:07:18.436
"And he wants me to be in the Olympics?" Brody liked the sound of that. "Cool!"

78
00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:27.932
But Julia was clearly worried. "We can't stay here," she told Brody. "We have to find a way home!"

79
00:07:27.933 --> 00:07:39.560
"Why the big rush?" Brody grinned. "If I get to be an Olympic champion, maybe I'll stick around!"

